WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
- Dr. House is out of
control, but so am I.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.410
Let's watch this episode. Bee-wop!

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.750
- [Operator] 911, what's your emergency?

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.290
- We got into an accident
along the Canal Road,

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:09.483
just outside Kingston.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.823
My mom's unconscious.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:13.580
- [Operator] Are you hurt?

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.610
- She should've asked,
"Does she have a pulse?

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.050
And if not, start chest compressions."

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.393
- I'm fine.

00:00:20.393 --> 00:00:21.226
- You're not fine.

00:00:21.226 --> 00:00:23.633
You have a metal object
going through your body.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.899
- Ow! Can we hurry this up?

00:00:27.899 --> 00:00:31.037
- We'll make sure that-
- Take your time.

00:00:31.037 --> 00:00:32.053
What's your name?

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:34.760
- Hannah Morganthal.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:38.340
- You have CIPA, Hannah Morganthal.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.277
- What is CIPA?

00:00:39.277 --> 00:00:40.580
- No, I don't.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.970
- We have to do x-rays to make sure

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.880
you don't have internal injuries,

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.440
blood tests to make sure no infections,

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.580
EEG for neurological anomalies,

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.940
and biopsy a spinal nerve.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.350
- I love how he just decided that,

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.190
because he didn't like
how she was responding

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.170
to the alcohol on her leg.

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:00.000
And first of all, who
puts alcohol on a leg?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.780
All you need is a little soapy water.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.380
Alcohol actually disrupts
the skin tissue there.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.730
- [Dr. Foreman] Only been
about 60 documented cases.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.580
- Yeah, and I have seven reasons

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.730
to think that she's one of them.

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.430
- Or she has meralgia paresthetica

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.720
and she's wearing a really tight belt.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.060
Come on, House, shape up!

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:16.750
- Reason number one,

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.770
she knew what it was
without us telling her.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.530
- That's true, but she could've
also been just acting tough,

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.660
you know, because some guy
challenged her, like you!

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.510
- Two, she's still wet from the snow.

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.460
But she's not shivering. That's odd.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.150
Unless she can't sweat
or feel hot and cold.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:32.886
- The ambulance was warm.

00:01:32.886 --> 00:01:33.990
I want to see my mother.

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.560
- Three, scarring around
the lips and tongue.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.393
When she was a baby,

00:01:37.393 --> 00:01:39.290
she chewed on herself without feeling it.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:40.990
- I fell through a
window when I was a kid.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:42.930
- Four, when you cleaned the wounds,

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.580
she flexed into the cleaner
instead of away from it.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.300
It's hard to fake pain
when you've never felt it.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.290
It takes an imaginative
leap, Ms. Morganthal.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:52.620
She wants to see her mom.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.970
If she admits having CIPA,

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.380
she knows we're not
letting her go anywhere

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.730
without a battery of tests.

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.420
- If she already knows she has CIPA,

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.400
why run the battery of tests?

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.470
I feel like House just likes
wasting hospital resources.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.500
- [Dr. Foreman] I'm
taking her to see her mom.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.810
She was-
(cane smacks)

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:10.480
- Imagine he's wrong and
he just hit a poor kid.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.530
Oh, why am I laughing?

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:14.120
- Is this a real case or
one of those imaginary cases

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:15.390
that happen when you're bored?

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.990
- CIPA.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:20.200
- CIPA is a diagnosis.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.870
Diagnoses happen at the end of cases.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:23.703
- Thank you.

00:02:23.703 --> 00:02:25.810
- She's got no idea what's
going on in her body.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.310
There's bound to be something wrong.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.180
- In other words, she
could be perfectly healthy,

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:31.940
but you're curious about
someone who can't feel pain

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:34.640
because you always feel pain
so you wanna go exploring.

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.850
- Or maybe because she has CIPA

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:39.420
and was just involved
in a major car accident,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.720
you should pan scan her and
make sure she doesn't have

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.620
internal bleeding or injuries,

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.890
which would be a very simple
test that House doesn't need

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.460
to be present for and he can go home.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.300
- She was in a car accident.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:52.700
She needs x-rays, blood
tests, EEG, nerve biopsy-

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.130
- What does she need an EEG for?

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.050
What are you looking for,

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:57.840
if she's having a seizure right now?

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.760
You can see if she's having a seizure.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.300
- Do your tests, except
for the nerve biopsy.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.310
- I need the nerve biopsy-
- You'd risk paralyzing her!

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.320
- What do you need a nerve biopsy for?

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.290
Again, if it's congenital, we know!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.770
There's no need looking
for a biopsy and a cause!

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:13.930
- If the EEG reveals a
problem, we can talk then.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.500
- But the EEG is not a defining test.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.410
The EEG is gonna show you brainwaves.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:19.670
Like, what is that gonna tell you?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.760
Maybe they meant an EMG?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.414
And they're just using the wrong acronym?

00:03:23.414 --> 00:03:24.980
(machine beeping)

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.550
That's an EEG. No idea
why they're doing it.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.050
- Spiking on leads C3 and O2.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.073
- She could be going into a seizure.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.017
- What is this? I don't understand.

00:03:34.017 --> 00:03:35.543
"She could be"? You can't see it?

00:03:35.543 --> 00:03:38.220
- What do you want us
to do, hold her down?

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.040
- Well, only until you
inject her with a sedative.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.230
Then you can let her go.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.690
- We tried.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:43.720
- Seriously?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.510
- She's strong and doesn't care.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:47.240
We'd have broken something
before we can get her

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.850
to sit still enough to inject her.

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.960
- So break her arm. She won't mind.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:52.793
- You're cranky.

00:03:52.793 --> 00:03:53.640
- I'm in pain.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.560
- And he's jealous of her
for not being in pain.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.260
Little does he know, a world without pain

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.810
is a much more dangerous
and problematic world

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.140
than with pain; ironic.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.070
- Every morning, I have to check my eyes

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:08.130
to make sure I didn't
scratch a cornea in my sleep.

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:11.580
- Oh God, stop. I'm in
a pool of tears here.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.610
- I can't cry!

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:13.803
- Neither can I.

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.700
Every morning I check
my eyes for jaundice,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.310
in case the Vicodin's
finally shot my liver.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:22.840
- I can't run anywhere without examining

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.580
all my toes for swelling.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:25.413
- I can't run.

00:04:25.413 --> 00:04:27.100
- It's opposite ends of the spectrum.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:31.193
Neither are good. That's
why we have homeostasis.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.160
- I'm sick?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.260
- No, your EEG was normal.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.950
X-ray showed no breaks, blood
test showed no infections,

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:41.319
urine indicated no...
(foreboding music)

00:04:41.319 --> 00:04:43.970
Hannah?
(machine beeping)

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:44.803
Call a code.

00:04:44.803 --> 00:04:46.220
- Okay, okay, okay.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:50.230
You do not call a code because
someone becomes unresponsive.

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:51.440
She could be having a seizure.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:52.980
You don't need to call a code.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.960
A code is when someone's heart stops.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.860
- Need ice packs and cooling blankets.

00:04:57.970 --> 00:04:58.803
- For what?

00:05:00.155 --> 00:05:00.988
(eyes boink)

00:05:00.988 --> 00:05:02.040
Do you know what the condition is?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.380
- She's not flushed, she's
not sweating. You must mean-

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:06.330
- She has a temperature of 105.

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.807
- How does she know?

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:08.850
(bell dings)
Oh, 'cause the thermometer

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:09.920
was still hanging out of her mouth?

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.470
Normally, if you are a healthy adult,

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.860
a fever will be controlled.

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.540
If you have a rare condition,
it can go out of control

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.510
and actually cause harm to your body.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:23.950
That is why I am a proponent
of, in certain instances,

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:27.910
decreasing the amount of
Tylenol, Advil, Motrin

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.950
that we give to patients
when they have a mild fever.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:34.430
Because a mild fever, generally
speaking, doesn't do harm.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:35.870
In fact, it allows your immune system

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:37.890
to work better and fight off infections,

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:39.890
make your symptoms go away faster,

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:41.480
improve your immune system,

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.340
make you spend less time being infectious,

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:45.750
infecting other people.

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:48.020
So like in this case,
this is the rare instance

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:50.160
where her fever can fry her brain.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.230
- What if we give her

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:54.860
more pain signals, a
lot more pain signals?

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:56.760
Maybe some of them will make it through.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:57.930
- You wanna torture her?

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:58.763
- No.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:02.930
Yes, if we do this to
anybody else, it's torture.

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:05.840
Doing it to her, it's no different
than pricking her finger.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.800
We keep poking sharp sticks into her,

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.537
eventually we'll find the
part that's already tender.

00:06:09.537 --> 00:06:12.030
- That's the most ridiculous
thing I ever heard of.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.510
On the off chance that maybe
she might feel something

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:16.070
and maybe we'll poke the right area.

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:17.490
What if it's internal?

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.023
What are you gonna do then, Chief?

00:06:19.023 --> 00:06:23.373
- This is warm, and the other is very hot.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.620
Start here, move to the hot one,

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.210
just a few seconds, then back.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.800
We're gonna monitor activity in your brain

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:31.633
while you do it.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.200
If you feel any response to the heat,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.075
it could indicate a vascular problem.

00:06:37.075 --> 00:06:38.430
- What?

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.860
- She's still in surgery.
They tell me it's going okay.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.470
You can take your hand out.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:44.220
- And you didn't ask anything else?

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.160
- [Dr. Chase] Take your
hand out of the water!

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.319
- What's going on with my mother?

00:06:49.319 --> 00:06:51.661
(suspenseful music)

00:06:51.661 --> 00:06:52.494
- Hannah!

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:56.703
You just got second degree burns.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.370
- Because you put her arm
in scalding water, Doctor!

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.400
- I didn't feel anything when you guys

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.070
screwed this thing into my head.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.940
- It'll replace missing
chemicals in your nerves,

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.063
heighten sensitivity.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.873
- What? On what planet?

00:07:10.873 --> 00:07:14.650
♪ This would never happen ♪

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:16.420
Oh my god, honestly,

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.650
I wish I was this girl
simply so I could sue

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.170
this hospital and become a billionaire.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:24.220
Judge, jury, they drilled into my skull

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.120
'cause maybe they thought I'd feel it.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.645
I win! That's it, I win.

00:07:29.645 --> 00:07:31.220
(machine beeping)

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.770
- So what, I just sit here while you guys

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:36.260
drill a hole in me?
(drill whirring)

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.220
- Just think about it.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.620
If they drill like a centimeter
too deep and hurt her brain

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:44.060
and she becomes functionally impaired...

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:50.670
Then what? Like, their pros
and cons of this are terrible!

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.793
- Stop the drill.
(Hannah screaming)

00:07:55.219 --> 00:07:59.720
(tool whirring)
(metal clattering)

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:03.120
It's okay. What'd you feel?
(Hannah whimpering)

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.160
Where did you feel it?

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:10.003
Hannah, I need to know how it hurt.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.110
- What just happened?

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:13.943
- Need you.

00:08:13.943 --> 00:08:14.870
- What did the nerve biopsy show?

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:15.703
- Never did it.

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:16.960
- Well then, do it!
- I can't!

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:17.793
- Why?

00:08:17.793 --> 00:08:20.180
- She's gonna jump off the lobby balcony.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.580
- You think I can catch her?

00:08:22.628 --> 00:08:25.128
(eerie music)

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.500
- House is an ass.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.100
But what did he expect
House to do there? (laughs)

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:34.470
Like, for real though,
like maybe call security?

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:36.570
I don't know, like-
- What do you want from us?

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.008
What do you want us to do?

00:08:38.008 --> 00:08:39.959
(suspenseful music)

00:08:39.959 --> 00:08:41.190
- I can't feel my legs!

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.320
- You're trying to pull the
same stunt twice in 10 minutes.

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.950
- I'm not pretending!

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.613
They don't hurt, they're just not there.

00:08:50.004 --> 00:08:55.004
(body crashes)
(frightening music)

00:08:57.770 --> 00:08:59.560
- They couldn't have
put something below her

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.810
so that if she did jump,

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.863
she would at least have a padded surface?

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:05.740
- Anything?

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:06.770
We're not looking for pain.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.150
Anything at all, pressure?

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.360
- Nothing.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.420
- You have six broken bones, a fever,

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.150
a concussion, erratic heart rhythms,

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:15.790
and a complete lack of
sensation below the waist.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.540
- I feel fine.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.540
- [Dr. House] Guilt.

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:21.928
- Guilt, as a symptom?

00:09:21.928 --> 00:09:23.430
- (laughs) I've never heard of that.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.930
- Alzheimer's can cause
euphoria, pain causes depression,

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:29.100
and B12 deficiency causes guilt.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.340
- If she had a B12 deficiency,
she would've been anemic.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.760
They would've seen that on the CBC.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:33.933
- Give her a shot of B12.

00:09:33.933 --> 00:09:36.840
When she gets better, I was right!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.240
- Or check her levels?
Like, I don't understand.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.153
- I'm not happy.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:43.860
Her white blood cell count was low,

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:47.560
and what she's got is just
a whole lot of eosinophils.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:51.603
- High eosinophils could be a
worm, a parasitic infection.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.283
- Is it possible for you
to just watch me eat,

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:00.730
or do you get some primeval thrill

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:03.173
out of beating the other
hunters to the food?

00:10:04.598 --> 00:10:07.860
(dramatic music)

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:09.170
- B12 deficiency.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.180
- Are you having deja vu?

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:11.500
We've had this conversation!

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.820
She was given B12. She didn't get better.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.610
- Oh, maybe she lacks
intrinsic factor to bind it.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.690
- 'Cause someone else ate it.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.200
Get an abdominal MRI.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.417
- What?

00:10:21.417 --> 00:10:23.906
- Oh, she has a worm!
- What are you doing?

00:10:23.906 --> 00:10:26.280
(suspenseful music)
(Hannah panting)

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:27.250
- 15.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.330
- You're not going to anesthetize her?

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.013
- Relax. It's just a magic trick.

00:10:32.685 --> 00:10:36.074
(Hannah screaming)

00:10:36.074 --> 00:10:37.370
She's faking it.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:38.870
We're not falling for it.
- "She's faking it!" (laughs)

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.280
Lake fishing can be fun.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:44.220
It can bring the generations together.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.493
If you don't cook that
trout or perch well,

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.083
you'll be giving room
and board to this fella.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:54.320
And by "free board," I mean
all the B12 you could take in.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.460
A tapeworm essentially starts feeding

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:58.000
on the foods that you're consuming,

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.860
so it literally takes
away nutrients from you.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:03.500
Most commonly, you can
get a B12 deficiency,

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.640
but then you would also
get a resulting anemia,

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.380
which is why this episode's
a little confusing,

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:08.950
'cause they said the CBC was normal

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:11.059
outside of a low white count.

00:11:11.059 --> 00:11:16.059
(suspenseful music)
(guts squishing)

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:17.560
- That's gotta be 25 feet long!

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.560
- Dammit, world record's over 60.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:24.430
- They didn't see the tapeworm

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.760
on all of the imaging that they did?

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:28.560
This girl's case is interesting

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.040
because she has this condition.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:33.920
She doesn't feel anything, therefore,

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.200
she's not aware of the tapeworm,
and that's not unusual.

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.180
A lot of people won't
be aware of a tapeworm.

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:42.120
But because she has this
tapeworm, was not getting B12,

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:45.610
she essentially started having
neurologic complications,

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:47.170
as well as having a fever,

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:49.590
because of the infestation of the worm,

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.840
and all these other symptoms popped up.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.280
But at the same time, they didn't pop up

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.750
like they normally would
in a healthy individual.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:57.810
Her presentation was masked

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.297
because she has the condition CIPA.

00:12:00.297 --> 00:12:03.587
"Detox Tea is a SCAM!" Click
here to check that out.

00:12:03.587 --> 00:12:05.400
"Wednesday Checkup"
video, it's a throwback.

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:07.857
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:12:07.857 --> 00:12:10.524
(upbeat music)

